// A flow the application limits keeps its window: twenty writes of 100 bytes, each acknowledged before the next,
// leave 100 bytes in flight at every send, never the window, and slow start grows only a window below twice the
// most in flight, 200. The initial window stands, ten segments of 1448, the peer's MSS of 1460 less the timestamp
// option, so a write of 20000 sends 14480. Growing on every ACK, as before, would have made the window
// 14480 + 20 * 100 = 16480. Linux grows only while tcp_is_cwnd_limited holds too: in packets, one in flight against
// a window of ten.
--congestion=newreno
0 socket(..., SOCK_STREAM, IPPROTO_TCP) = 3
+0 bind(3, ..., ...) = 0
+0 listen(3, 1) = 0

+0 < S 0:0(0) win 65535 <mss 1460,nop,nop,TS val 100 ecr 0>
+0 > S. 0:0(0) ack 1 win 65535 <mss 1460,nop,nop,TS val 0 ecr 100>
+0 < . 1:1(0) ack 1 win 65535 <nop,nop,TS val 100 ecr 0>
+0 accept(3, ..., ...) = 4

+0 write(4, ..., 100) = 100
